# The AASA and assetlinks files are stored at repo root and exposed at their
# canonical /.well-known/ URLs via rewrite (status 200, not 301 — Apple/Google
# fetch the path verbatim and won't follow redirects). This root+rewrite layout
# is kept because it is proven live against Apple's CDN and Google's verifier —
# NOT because Pages hides dotdirs (it does not; see CLAUDE.md, 2026-08-30).
/.well-known/apple-app-site-association   /apple-app-site-association   200
/.well-known/assetlinks.json              /assetlinks.json              200
# security.txt (RFC 9116) — same arrangement: stored at root, exposed at its canonical path.
/.well-known/security.txt                 /security.txt                 200

# SPA fallback — keep last so the rules above match first.
/*                                        /index.html                   200
